From 1f45d78199a9af6d6fe3c80c3ea83467844a4579 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:48:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 129/130] hir: the expression visitor visits a lowered async
 block's captures

tokio 1.43.0 (sad 0.4.32) sync/watch.rs:1241:

    pub async fn closed(&self) {
        cooperative(async { .. while self.receiver_count() > 0 { .. notified.await; } }).await;
    }

Coroutines are lowered innermost first. A lowered async block keeps its
uses of outer variables as capture nodes (m_captures), but
ExprVisitorDef skipped them (a lowered generator's are visited), so the
enclosing coroutine's variable renumbering never reached them. The inner
block then captured slot 0 of the original function, which in the outer
coroutine's poll is `self`: "MIR ERROR: <future#I_closed_581<'I0,T> as
Future>::poll BB9/0: ensure_valid: Use of non-valid lvalue - _0" (before
0128, a type mismatch `&mut future#outer` vs `&mut async[..]`). This is
the long-open "await an async block inside an async fn" case
(`let b = async move { x }; b.await`).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/hir/expr.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/hir/expr.cpp b/src/hir/expr.cpp
index 15bc97a0..7b4b05d9 100644
--- a/src/hir/expr.cpp
+++ b/src/hir/expr.cpp
@@ -328,6 +328,12 @@ DEF_VISIT_H(ExprNode_AsyncBlock, node) {
     }
     else
     {
+        // Lowered: the captures are the block's uses of outer variables (as for a generator), so an enclosing
+        // coroutine's variable rewrite must see them
+        // - tokio 1.43.0 sync/oneshot.rs `closed`, or `async fn f(x: u8) -> u8 { let b = async move { x }; b.await }`:
+        //   the inner block still captured slot 0 of the function, which in the outer coroutine's poll is `self`
+        for(auto& cap : node.m_captures)
+            visit_node_ptr(cap);
     }
 }
 
